@startuml db_schema
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10

title DEAP-bridge — Service Database Schema (SQLite, _service.db)

entity "experiments" as experiments {
  * **id** : TEXT <<PK>>
  ..
  * label : TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''
  * spec_json : TEXT NOT NULL <<JSON>>
  * status : TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued'
  ..
  * created_at : REAL NOT NULL <<unix epoch>>
  started_at : REAL
  finished_at : REAL
  ..
  run_dirs_json : TEXT <<JSON array>>
  progress_json : TEXT <<JSON>>
  error : TEXT
  pid : INTEGER
  ..
  * enqueue_seq : INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
  * origin : TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ui'
  ..
  <b>CHECK</b> status IN
    (queued, running, completed,
     failed, cancelled)
  <b>CHECK</b> origin IN (ui, cli, import)
  ..
  <b>INDEX</b> idx_status (status)
  <b>INDEX</b> idx_enqueue_seq (enqueue_seq)
}

entity "queue_state" as queue_state {
  * **id** : INTEGER <<PK>>
  ..
  * paused : INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 <<bool>>
  * worker_limit : INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
  ..
  <b>CHECK</b> id = 1  <i>(singleton row)</i>
}

package "Results store (filesystem, not the database)" as FS {
  class "experiments/{id}/" as ExpDir <<artifact>> {
    _spec.json
    _stdout.log
    _progress.json
    _result.json
  }
  class "{run_dir}/" as RunDir <<artifact>> {
    manifest.json
    metrics.csv
    summary.json
    probe.csv
    checkpoints/
    frames/
  }
}

queue_state ||..o{ experiments : gates dispatch

experiments ||-down-|| ExpDir
experiments ||-down-o{ RunDir

note right of experiments
  <b>Status state machine</b>
  queued -> running -> completed | failed | cancelled

  <i>queued -> running</i> is a single atomic
  <i>UPDATE ... RETURNING</i> gated on the queue being
  unpaused and no row already running, so no two
  dispatch polls can claim the same experiment.

  The terminal states are write-once: later updates
  are guarded by a <i>WHERE status NOT IN (...)</i> clause
  naming the three terminal states.

  On restart, rows left in <i>running</i> are re-queued
  rather than failed — a stale row means the server
  stopped, not that the experiment did.
end note

note bottom of queue_state
  A single-row table rather than a
  configuration file, so pausing the
  queue and the queue contents commit
  in the same transactional store.

  <i>paused</i> is read inside the dispatch
  claim itself, so a pause takes effect
  atomically rather than racing the next
  poll. <i>worker_limit</i> is persisted as a seam
  for future concurrency; the claim
  currently hard-gates on no experiment
  already running.
end note

note bottom of FS
  <b>Deliberate split.</b> The database holds only
  what must be queried and mutated transactionally
  — queue order and lifecycle state. Experiment
  results are immutable, large and heterogeneous
  (CSV, JSON, checkpoints, video), so they stay on
  the shared volume and are referenced by path.

  This keeps the schema stable while result
  artefacts evolve, and lets the frontend read
  results directly from a read-only mount instead
  of streaming them through the API.

  One experiment owns exactly one experiment
  directory (keyed by <i>id</i>) and zero or more run
  directories — one per sub-run, i.e. per
  algorithm x seed — whose paths are held
  denormalised in <i>run_dirs_json</i>.
end note

note left of experiments::spec_json
  Stored as a JSON document rather than
  normalised into tables: the experiment
  spec is an open, plugin-extensible
  structure whose hyperparameter set is
  defined by the catalog, not by the
  database. It is validated by Pydantic
  at the API boundary before insertion.
end note

@enduml
